      <Comment source="pmngroup">The gene encoding the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; protein CYP710A2 was recombinantly expressed in insect cells. Microsomal fractions were used to characterize the substrate specificity and the C-22 desaturation activity of the enzyme |CITS:[16531502]|. The enzyme was shown to catalyze the C-22 desaturation of |FRAME:CPD-4143| and |FRAME:CPD-8134|, but not that of |FRAME:CPD-707|. The activity of the enzyme was too low to allow for the reproducible determination of its kinetic parameters |CITS:[16531502]|.</Comment>
